# Same menus cell (820x1180,touch, carried/fresh). README's battleground
# section: "a team of five is exact... tap a tank into your own slot and the
# slot that was tanking takes the one you gave up." No prior session has
# actually tapped a role slot on the battleground party screen to see the
# trade happen -- only ui-checked it for size/overlap. Quick, cheap check.
open
tap battleground
tap map:conquest
tap compose
targets
ui
shot bgcompose

# Bastion is "H Druid Heal" and Wren is "T Druid Tank" going in. Tap Bastion's
# slot and give them a tank spec instead -- README says the slot that WAS
# tanking (Wren) should take the role Bastion gave up (healer), rather than
# the composition ending up with two tanks and no healer.
tap slot:1
targets
shot bgcompose-picker
tap spec:paladin:protection
targets
shot bgcompose-after-swap

# Also: is "THE RAID" the real header on a 5-person battleground team, or did
# the earlier `shot` just crop it oddly? Confirm by reading state directly.
state
